WEBVTT

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.610
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.220
Elise...

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.630
<b>The Dancing Girl</b>

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.090
You won't let me keep writing?

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:59.830
Do you still resent me?

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.610
Elise...

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.160
If you refuse to let me write...

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.900
Then so be it.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.570
The moon will be full soon,

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.580
and she will disappear from me

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.620
just as quickly as she appeared

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.720
on the night of the last full moon.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.460
I am out of time.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.990
I have run out of time.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.700
<b>Escaping at 3 O'Clock in the Afternoon</b>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.200
Meow, meow, mreow-mreow-mreow?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.130
Meow, meow?

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.240
What are you doing?

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.020
I'm asking if he knows a black cat.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.870
See, he looks just like Pork Loin 
from Fujita-san's house.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.310
Meow?

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.220
Can he even understand you?

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.220
He can! He can understand 
my feelings, at least.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.790
<i>He can understand my feelings.</i>

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:34.220
If that's what you really want to do, 
then you should stay.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:41.170
<i>Yes. I will keep waiting for you, Ougai-san.</i>

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.130
Little Squirrel.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.960
Would you like to go indulge 
in some sweets with me?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.090
You too, of course, Syunso.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.480
Yes! Gladly!

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.710
Why didn't Syunso join us, I wonder?

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.970
Well, he mentioned something about
 his stomach suddenly hurting.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.340
All right, then.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.480
We'll be going now, Syunso-san!

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.990
<i>You seem so happy and full of smiles</i>

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:29.250
<i>whenever Ougai-san is around...</i>

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.750
So, Tatsuno-san, why does Tokyo Station
use header bond brickwork?

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.760
Tokyo Station? Are you referring 
to the Tokyo Railway Station?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.200
I am still working on the design for it,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.660
but what did you just say 
about header bond brickwork?

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.890
I was just thinking that erecting such a large 
building with header bond brickwork would be unusual.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.410
Wait, that's actually a good idea.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.020
Thank you for the food!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.050
So does the header bond with facing bricks?

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.520
It's absolutely scrumptious!

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.020
You really seem to be enjoying it.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:09.090
Getting to see how much you 
enjoy it is enough for me.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.880
No way, that's silly.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:15.310
So, Ougai-san, how goes the 
progress on your novel?

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.480
Maybe I shouldn't have asked about it?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.790
Y-You know,

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:26.280
Yakumo-san calls Fujita-san's 
place Café Fujita.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.540
He has a dish there called the Goro Special, 
and it looks really good.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:35.570
Indeed, your expression of 
delight is truly delicious.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.550
<i>I-I probably shouldn't ask 
him about his novel.</i>

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.830
I wonder if Otojiro-san will end up

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.070
playing the role of Shirayuki in 
that play Kyoka-san wrote?

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.830
I'm really glad he was able to 
finish writing it so soon.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.820
Oh, I-I'm so sorry! I-I wasn't thinking...

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.840
You finally have a chance 
to relax. I'm sorry.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.030
Would you like to order some red 
bean soup as well, Little Squirrel?

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.800
I-Is that all right?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.830
Of course.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.600
It's so sweet! I'm so happy!

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:31.560
I... am thinking about quitting writing.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:37.750
Huh?

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:39.080
Y...

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:44.450
You mean as a profession?

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.650
I can't write.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.060
Besides...

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.400
You are right here with me now,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.890
and I think that is more than enough.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.630
I'm glad to hear that, but...

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:24.490
I thought you would be more pleased.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.180
I'll try doing the framework 
in the British style.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:32.380
British style? That sounds like chaos!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:34.400
But I would like to read it.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.800
I would like to read your novel, Ougai-san.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.870
So...

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:48.560
I can't write it.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:09.760
I know...

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:16.800
...that it's probably rather 
impertinent for me to say this,

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:22.380
since I can't do anything and 
I don't know anything...

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:29.200
But I want you to keep writing 
your novel, Ougai-san.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:37.910
Quitting in the middle just 
doesn't seem like you...

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.920
Hey...

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:01.890
Syunso-san?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.430
Got a minute?

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.340
The story Ougai-san 
is trying to write...

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.820
It's...

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.360
about him and his former lover.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:54.720
Ougai-san is trying to write 
a novel about the lover

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.170
he met while studying abroad.

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:04.780
They met in Germany and fell in love.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:08.410
They considered spending 
the rest of their lives together.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:10.710
But...

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.310
Since Ougai-san had studied abroad 
for the sake of his country,

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.920
those around him were 
against him marrying her.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:24.640
He was only permitted to live as 
a public figure, not as an individual.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:31.700
And so Ougai-san decided 
to break it off with her.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.180
Elise...

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:44.720
I believe he regrets that, even now.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.670
Elise... I know.

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:54.100
I know you will not let me write.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.570
I assure you...

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:01.110
I have quit writing altogether.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:03.860
So please...

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.190
Stop appearing to me!

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.670
Elise...

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:21.450
That story traces the path of 
why his heart was closed off.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.550
That's why he can't write it.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:31.780
Why is he trying to write 
such a painful story?

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:34.830
For you.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:41.220
Ougai-san is currently 
trying to face his past.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:47.040
He is doing it for you,
because you're here now.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:57.580
He's putting himself through 
all that suffering... for me?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.030
Ougai-san...?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.550
<b>The Dancing Girl</b>

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:21.590
Hey!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.770
Oh, Mei-san.

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:31.880
Fumi-san!

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.900
I saw Ougai-san just now.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:39.970
We passed one another over there, 
but when I tried to call out to him,

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:43.720
it was like he couldn't hear. 
He was completely out of it.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.080
Thank you so much, Fumi-san!

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.110
Ougai-san!

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:04.980
<i>Ougai-san!</i>

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.330
Ougai-san!

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.850
Can I help you?

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.770
Oh, pardon me!

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.720
Well now, you're quite the looker.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:18.910
I was mistaken!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.730
What are you doing?

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:39.510
I might have driven Ougai-san away.

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:42.770
All because I didn't know anything!

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:46.530
Even if that's true, Ougai-san 
is not such a weak person.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:49.520
Y-You may be right.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.940
But still...

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:57.220
I can't just do nothing while 
Ougai-san is suffering.

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:02.040
I can't stand to see you like this!

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:16.450
Thank you, Syunso-san.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.060
I am fine now.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:33.230
<i>I'm fine. I'm fine.</i>

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.300
Mei!

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.230
You are...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.720
an illusion that I've created.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.180
You are the very weakness of my heart.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.080
I knew that from the beginning.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:39.000
I thought you would disappear 
if I stopped writing, though.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:41.850
Elise...

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:44.890
I never imagined...

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:55.250
that facing you would 
bring me this much pain.

00:16:55.900 --> 00:17:00.180
I give up, Elise. I won't write anymore.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:02.250
No...

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.900
I can't write.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:14.090
I never thought that I was so pathetic

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:18.570
that I wouldn't be able to 
face either my past or my present.

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.730
Elise...

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.590
Ougai-san!

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.650
Thank goodness.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.400
I finally found you!

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:48.250
Please don't look at me while I'm like this.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:56.120
I love you even when 
you're upset, Ougai-san.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.730
I truly do.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.840
I will read it.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:11.090
No matter what the story is,
 or how sad it may be.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:15.700
No, I can't...

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.700
You can write it!

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:20.710
I am positive that you can write it.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:25.930
It is the story that you struggled 
so hard and suffered for.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:30.450
I am absolutely certain that 
it will be a wonderful story.

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:43.490
And if... And if you absolutely...

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:48.960
Absolutely cannot do it, Ougai-san,

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:50.970
you can just

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:55.000
escape from it with me.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.990
We'll go somewhere nice, like a hot spring.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.370
Mei...

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.340
Yes?

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.250
Stay with me forever, Mei.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:22.430
Stay by my side forever.

00:19:23.190 --> 00:19:25.380
Yes, I will.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:31.020
I will always be by your side.

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:46.960
<i>Mei, you are incredibly strong.</i>

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:02.050
This fell on the study floor.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:24.560
Elise...

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.130
You finished writing it!

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:21.430
I did.

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:28.090
And it is entirely thanks to you, Mei.

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:30.920
Thank you.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:33.680
I didn't really do anything,

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:36.770
but it makes me glad to hear you say that.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.640
I'm looking forward to reading it.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.400
No, you don't get to read it, Little Squirrel.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.840
What? Why not?

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:52.530
I am going to find the black cat.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:56.410
I want to see your finished painting!

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.420
<i>I'm sure I can paint it now.</i>

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.260
My eyes...!

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Next Episode Preview

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Chat Noir Won't Look Back

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:31.970
Syunso-san...

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.680
If having the surgery means 
you can get better, I...

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:39.920
There's no guarantee I'll get 
better if I have the surgery.
